  <title>Assembled products</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Assembled products</gui></guiseq> keeps the
  bill of materials of each manufactured product: the parts, and how many of
  each, that go into one. Manufacturing uses it to take the parts out of
  stock. Changes are saved as you make them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the manufactured product. <gui>Manufactured products</gui>
    opens the products window showing them, to add a new one.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Version</gui> of its parts list.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New Item</gui>, or press <key>F2</key>, and type the
    <gui>Qty</gui>, choose the <gui>Product</gui> and add a
    <gui>Remark</gui>. If the part is already on the list you are asked
    whether to update its quantity or add it again. The <gui>Qty</gui> can be
    a sum such as <input>2x12</input>; see
    <link xref="qty_arithmetic"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Delete Item</gui>, or <key>F3</key>, removes the selected
    part.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p><gui>Total items :</gui> and <gui>Total Cost :</gui> add up the list at
  the parts' current costs. <gui>Notes</gui> are kept with the version.
  Right click a part for its <gui>Product hub</gui>. You can also drag
  products onto the list.</p>

  <section id="versions">
  <title>Versions</title>
  <p>When a product's design changes, make a new version of its parts list
  rather than changing the old one, so what was made before still shows what
  it used. Click <gui>Version</gui> to open the <gui>Product Assembly
  Version</gui> window:</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Name</gui> of the new version. Check <gui>Use
    assembly items from version</gui> and choose one to start from a copy of
    its parts and notes. Click <gui>Create version</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click a version's name to rename it. Uncheck <gui>Active</gui> to
    retire it.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

  <section id="menu">
  <title>The window menu</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Export list to CSV file</gui></title>
    <p>Saves the parts list to a spreadsheet file, with each part's order
    number from the vendor you choose, for ordering the parts.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Products</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="products">products</link> window.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

